      "content": "### Introduction to Python Loops: Cheat Sheet for Beginners\n\n**For Loop:**\n- Uses a `for` keyword to iterate over a sequence (like a list, tuple, or range).\n```python\nfor i in range(5):\n    print(i)  # Outputs numbers 0 to 4\n```\n\n**While Loop:**\n- Executes a block of code as long as a condition is true.\n```python\ni = 0\nwhile i < 5:\n    print(i)\n    i += 1  # Increment or Decrement\n```\n\n**Iteration:**\n- The act of repeating a block of code.\n\n**range():**\n- Function returning a sequence of numbers.\n```python\nfor i in range(5):  # Generates numbers from 0 to 4\n    print(i)\n```\n\n**increment:**\n- Typically used to increase a loop counter.\n```python\nfor i in range(5):\n    i += 1  # Manually incrementing i\n```\n\n**decrement:**\n- Decreases the value of a loop variable.\n\n**loop variable:**\n- A variable used to keep track of iteration, e.g., `i`, `j`.\n\n**break:**",
