      "content": "### Comprehensive Introduction to Python Loops Cheat Sheet\n\n**For Loop:**\n\nA `for` loop in Python is used for iteration. The `for` loop goes through a sequence, like a list, tuple, range, string, or other iterable objects. The syntax of a `for` loop is as follows:\n```python\nfor loop variable in iterable:\n    body of the loop\n```\n\n**For Example:**\n```python\nfor i in range(5):\n    print(i)  # Outputs sequence of numbers 0, 1, 2, 3, 4\n```\n\nThis snippet demonstrates iterating over a range object, which is an example of an iterable. Notice how the loop variable `i` serves as the iterator. This example reinforces the concept of iteration, a central aspect of understanding loops.\n\n**Role of iteration:**\nIteration is the act of repeating a block of code. In a `for` loop, the iterator variable cycles through each item in the sequence. After each complete loop, the iterator updates its value to the next item. This pattern continues until the sequence is exhausted, showcasing the principle of iteration.\n\n**Understanding the range() function:**\nThe `range()` function is commonly used",
